{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Java code to GNU C++11 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following Java 8 code to GNU C++11 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original Java 8 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n<your_rewritten_code_5>\nimport java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        BufferedReader br = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n        String[] input = br.readLine().split(\" \");\n        int a = Integer.parseInt(input[0]);\n        int b = Integer.parseInt(input[1]);\n        int l = Integer.parseInt(input[2]) - 1;\n        int r = Integer.parseInt(input[3]) - 1;\n        \n        int minDistinct = 26;\n        \n        for (char p = 'a'; p <= 'z'; p++) {\n            for (char q = (char)('a' + a); q <= 'z'; q++) {\n                String pattern = createPattern(a, b, p, q);\n                int distinct = getDistinctCount(pattern, l, r);\n                if (distinct < minDistinct) minDistinct = distinct;\n            }\n        }\n        \n        System.out.println(minDistinct);\n    }\n    \n    private static String createPattern(int a, int b, char p, char q) {\n        StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder();\n        \n        for (int i = 0; i < a; i++) {\n            sb.append((char)('a' + i));\n        }\n        \n        for (int i = 0; i < b; i++) {\n            sb.append(p);\n        }\n        \n        for (int i = 0; i < a; i++) {\n            boolean[] used = new boolean[26];\n            int start = b;\n            int end = b + a + i;\n            \n            for (int j = start; j < end && j < sb.length(); j++) {\n                used[sb.charAt(j) - 'a'] = true;\n            }\n            \n            for (int j = 0; j < 26; j++) {\n                if (!used[j]) {\n                    sb.append((char)('a' + j));\n                    break;\n                }\n            }\n        }\n        \n        for (int i = 0; i < b; i++) {\n            sb.append(q);\n        }\n        \n        return sb.toString();\n    }\n    \n    private static int getDistinctCount(String pattern, int l, int r) {\n        boolean[] seen = new boolean[26];\n        int len = pattern.length();\n        int range = r - l + 1;\n        \n        if (range >= 100000) {\n            for (int i = 0; i < len; i++) {\n                seen[pattern.charAt(i) - 'a'] = true;\n            }\n        } else {\n            for (int i = l; i <= r; i++) {\n                seen[pattern.charAt(i % len) - 'a'] = true;\n            }\n        }\n        \n        int count = 0;\n        for (boolean b : seen) {\n            if (b) count++;\n        }\n        return count;\n    }\n}\n</your_rewritten_code_5>\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <string>\n#include <vector>\n#include <algorithm>\n#include <climits>\n\nusing namespace std;\n\nstring createPattern(int a, int b, char p, char q) {\n    string sb = \"\";\n    \n    for (int i = 0; i < a; i++) {\n        sb += (char)('a' + i);\n    }\n    \n    for (int i = 0; i < b; i++) {\n        sb += p;\n    }\n    \n    for (int i = 0; i < a; i++) {\n        vector<bool> used(26, false);\n        int start = b;\n        int end = b + a + i;\n        \n        for (int j = start; j < end && j < (int)sb.length(); j++) {\n            used[sb[j] - 'a'] = true;\n        }\n        \n        for (int j = 0; j < 26; j++) {\n            if (!used[j]) {\n                sb += (char)('a' + j);\n                break;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    \n    for (int i = 0; i < b; i++) {\n        sb += q;\n    }\n    \n    return sb;\n}\n\nint getDistinctCount(string pattern, int l, int r) {\n    vector<bool> seen(26, false);\n    int len = pattern.length();\n    int range = r - l + 1;\n    \n    if (range >= 100000) {\n        for (int i = 0; i < len; i++) {\n            seen[pattern[i] - 'a'] = true;\n        }\n    } else {\n        for (int i = l; i <= r; i++) {\n            seen[pattern[i % len] - 'a'] = true;\n        }\n    }\n    \n    int count = 0;\n    for (bool b : seen) {\n        if (b) count++;\n    }\n    return count;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    string line;\n    getline(cin, line);\n    \n    vector<int> input;\n    string num = \"\";\n    for (char c : line) {\n        if (c == ' ') {\n            if (!num.empty()) {\n                input.push_back(stoi(num));\n                num = \"\";\n            }\n        } else {\n            num += c;\n        }\n    }\n    if (!num.empty()) {\n        input.push_back(stoi(num));\n    }\n    \n    int a = input[0];\n    int b = input[1];\n    int l = input[2] - 1;\n    int r = input[3] - 1;\n    \n    int minDistinct = 26;\n    \n    for (char p = 'a'; p <= 'z'; p++) {\n        for (char q = (char)('a' + a); q <= 'z'; q++) {\n            string pattern = createPattern(a, b, p, q);\n            int distinct = getDistinctCount(pattern, l, r);\n            if (distinct < minDistinct) minDistinct = distinct;\n        }\n    }\n    \n    cout << minDistinct << endl;\n    \n    return 0;\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.0003026